lane: segments-two-consumers
why: correctness defect in landed code (channel-ring-unbounded).
  Segments.popMany re-derives the run's segment AFTER winning the CAS,
  via segmentFor(headSeg, ...). With TWO consumers the other one can
  advance headSeg past our claimed run in between, and the
  hint-is-ahead fallback cannot help because the hint IS headSeg -- so
  the read walks a later segment, taking wrong values or hitting a
  null slot. The consumer dies with an unlogged exception inside a
  virtual thread and the law spins for ever waiting on its counter.
  Found by dumping a 19-minute 99%-CPU process rather than killing it.
how: keep the segment the SCAN used instead of re-deriving it. It is
  the segment of `pos`, obtained before the CAS was won, and segments
  are never freed, so holding the reference is enough. Plus a
  two-consumer test on Segments directly, and the law must stop
  swallowing a dead consumer.
